{"skill":{"slug":"hippocampus-memory","displayName":"Hippocampus"},"version":{"version":"3.8.6","createdAt":1770323640353,"changelog":"- Skill name updated to \"hippocampus-memory\" and title clarified.\n- Description rewritten for clarity and conciseness.\n- Metadata version bumped to 3.8.6.\n- Documentation restructured for easier reading; headings clarified and formatting improved.\n- No changes to scripts, features, or usage—documentation improvements only.","changelogSource":"auto","license":null,"files":[{"path":"ARCHITECTURE.md","size":8252,"sha256":"1402486aa8cae1e8e5bb2f0199b3e085ff7c10d931352fa20d2534032817c2e9","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"CHANGELOG.md","size":1908,"sha256":"ce6bc77fe925e33c5be9c58a5b42fe8e2bd9b5c456e662e8232718879c4ad354","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"CONFIG-UPGRADE.md","size":1896,"sha256":"1101792a5e75f40a5111d15952cb758488551b149dbda45c2314271d7cb0cc9d","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"README.md","size":5975,"sha256":"31a5f315177c949e64261d606bc5ff7eac3d9347e903406b55ab83c5eda87cbe","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"SKILL.md","size":7753,"sha256":"a958020dd34fdd52527191bc679bd015aa210d319c714131b254adf435d3db32","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"agentdir/AGENTS.md","size":4075,"sha256":"422622e88371244bb61414a884ca00f87a615713615e3a3d0a481e95f963fee7","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"agents/hippocampus-agent.md","size":3568,"sha256":"8506b0b7db1b233ca04374f65ba1f3318579ed7258e080ae5d375da56f13b16b","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"install.sh","size":7328,"sha256":"faace53d035309a51bf2a24377d47b8ce4983640adf78f4622159d504d5269ad","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"prompts/consolidation-guide.md","size":1734,"sha256":"4e49e3611c4f65986b8a782b5d82c1c9c68e9d740fad88593d7c8dd96cdd54a1","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"prompts/deep-inquiry.md","size":2082,"sha256":"65556a77275822837da9b491dc3c1d155b2ed1c2790800f1daa5b8bc2a6442e8","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"prompts/encode-signals.md","size":330,"sha256":"b4fdd9d8b836374690e7accc87213d41674323f97067669667bf5a162630368e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"prompts/process-recent.md","size":1208,"sha256":"c1189c2a5fefb1e0add73a2bb18128bc453e9c320451497827c37792de97c4d7","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"prompts/recall-patterns.md","size":1770,"sha256":"ee5ecf44dec59212d5924b0f1f25fe61ea2bb38b3a576d51627d37f82b169b64","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"prompts/relationship-detection.md","size":1514,"sha256":"bd9b9ded94356dce32240fe3df540f655fc7c3dbcf9b88dcf4eb6eae5ad98288","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"prompts/self-reflect.md","size":1216,"sha256":"5e524ff3fb022d5225da1849b5e8e7d4e70071f8462d9d4b04cd4acd74a56256","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"prompts/weekly-reflection-event.md","size":609,"sha256":"f58ba17e6ce0adac870c627b670d5b459cacf827447ce341a10ea5325563b827","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"scripts/consolidate.sh","size":1218,"sha256":"0c9541849912ea7a09ef5282ddecad79456b9acb67f62be815b5891336f9ac9b","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/decay.sh","size":3383,"sha256":"746cc67f3e9d08179ac04a1c6f99713f0d7be8f751937e4d5a9209057b599569","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/encode-pipeline.sh","size":9432,"sha256":"b9a56f45cdef2d97510a67bae01f1b7896457ad754df4323dbef747a72a8b9b8","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/generate-dashboard.sh","size":24051,"sha256":"5dd61b607a83dbf87f9aa477e31efc1d7768e3de8524e2f11dc5a62e7735e82e","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/load-core.sh","size":1454,"sha256":"c20b285e1fe83e32aec98192a10b5171daecaaea204009c3c3e5145033ae91cc","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/preprocess.sh","size":7769,"sha256":"f295c0134e0257488632a81437ea2322b0e5c77b457a28c97f001c24c58cf77e","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/recall.sh","size":3052,"sha256":"93231ac87926d9c1212f1f494d1d10df66b6d3d6610c8c00fb73be34912d1235","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/reflect.sh","size":829,"sha256":"9e19cb263d214342f9103258949bfa188f98e0bf8cbd772fe9d625cd1f4d2898","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/summarize-pending.sh","size":4338,"sha256":"df8acba3513a7d6cf9088f8e4ef05bf191c2ac7918cdd7ac6fa66abe37494559","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"scripts/sync-core.sh","size":2091,"sha256":"4d9c2ecf524239689785abcf83d6058fa3f982d3023e0222808105cecef6dafa","contentType":"application/x-sh"},{"path":"templates/daily.md","size":165,"sha256":"efb67ed0018af1f60bd5eb2740cf6089ea803eefe918abbc8fddbe2843917f0e","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2671,"sha256":"f3b06c2d01a7500fb6d159382b947f9383c8f11085c1797fed05bb6b1aa6b80c","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789025695997,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"dddd2f3868451b11c804f774349f801e6ad964b424fef44e544cdbbf90938a0f","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/dddd2f3868451b11c804f774349f801e6ad964b424fef44e544cdbbf90938a0f","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: \nDeveloper: \nVersion: \nDescription: OpenClaw Agent Skill\nSuspicious High-Entropy/Eval files: 10\n\nThe OpenClaw Hippocampus skill is designed to provide persistent memory for AI agents by processing conversation history. Its core functionality involves reading all session transcripts (`preprocess.sh`), storing and managing memories in `index.json` within the agent's workspace, and running cron jobs for encoding and decay. While accessing conversation history is a sensitive operation, it is fundamental to the skill's stated purpose. The instructions for the AI agent (found in `SKILL.md`, `install.sh`'s `--agent-turn` arguments, `summarize-pending.sh`, and `agents/hippocampus-agent.md`) are detailed but consistently focused on memory management tasks, without any evidence of intentional harmful behavior, data exfiltration to external endpoints, or unauthorized system manipulation. All observed capabilities, including file access and agent instructions, are plausibly and transparently aligned with the benign objective of building an AI memory system.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779160543840},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":100,"severity":"CRITICAL","recommendation":"DO_NOT_INSTALL","issueCount":62,"checkedAt":1789025695997},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This memory skill is purpose-aligned but needs review because it persistently scans and stores conversations, can run on a schedule, and contains exploitable local scripting and dashboard-rendering bugs.","dimensions":[{"detail":"The skill reads all JSONL session transcripts for the selected OpenClaw agent, writes plaintext intermediate and long-term memory files under the workspace, and generates a dashboard from memory and related brain-skill state without documented retention, deletion, filtering, or file-permission safeguards.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The manifest install path recommends running install.sh with cron, and the installer can add recurring encoding and decay cron jobs, chmod scripts, initialize memory files, generate dashboard output, and recommend automatic RAG loading; no remote payload retrieval was found.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The instructions disclose memory capture and recall, but raw transcript-derived signals are presented adjacent to agent instructions for summarization, creating a prompt-injection path into persistent memory; self-reflection prompts also encourage durable agent self-concept formation.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Persistence is central to the purpose, but it is high impact: cron jobs continue processing over time, HIPPOCAMPUS_CORE.md is intended for future context loading, unquoted heredocs allow Python code injection through parameters such as recall queries or thresholds, and dashboard content is rendered unsafely with innerHTML.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The package coherently implements a persistent OpenClaw memory system, but it captures user, relationship, emotional, and agent-identity facts into long-lived memory and core context; the claimed default limit of the last 100 signals is not enforced by the encoding pipeline on a fresh install.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only after reviewing the privacy and scripting risks. Avoid enabling cron or whole-history processing unless you explicitly want historical conversations summarized into persistent plaintext memory. Do not use this around secrets or sensitive personal data until the code-injection, prompt-injection, dashboard escaping, retention, permissions, approval, and deletion controls are fixed.","findings":"[SQP-2] expected: Persistent storage of conversation-derived memories is expected for this skill, but the artifacts support the concern that emotional, relationship, and personal facts are stored without clear consent, minimization, retention, or deletion controls.\n[SSD-3] expected: Capturing salient conversation facts is purpose-aligned, but the capture rules intentionally prioritize sensitive emotional and relationship content, and preprocessing scans all session files for the selected agent.\n[RA2] expected: Background and scheduled persistence are disclosed as core behavior, so this is not inherently rogue, but it materially increases privacy and governance risk and should be reviewed before installation.\n[T02] unexpected: The artifact-backed memory-poisoning concern is valid: transcript text is treated as summarization input and can be promoted into index.json and HIPPOCAMPUS_CORE.md without a robust instruction/data boundary or approval step.\n[T09] unexpected: The unquoted heredoc pattern in recall.sh, load-core.sh, sync-core.sh, summarize-pending.sh, and decay.sh creates real local code-injection risk when attacker-controlled or environment-controlled values are interpolated into Python source.\n[T09] unexpected: The generated dashboard embeds unescaped identity and memory-derived content into HTML and JavaScript and later uses innerHTML, supporting the stored HTML/JavaScript injection finding.\n[TP4] expected: The broad description is not deceptive for the package as a whole because the artifacts include encoding, decay, recall, sync, and dashboard components, though some individual helper scripts are narrower and the stated first-run signal limit is not actually wired into encode-pipeline.sh.\n[LP3] expected: Shell, local file access, and cron are expected for this implementation, but the skill does not define a narrow permissions boundary despite requiring broad local transcript and workspace mutation authority.\n[SQP-3] unexpected: The self-reflection and deep-inquiry prompts are ancillary to memory operation and encourage durable agent identity, opinions, desire, and continuity in ways that are not necessary for a safe memory utility.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789025695997}}}}}